            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "rotateLog in engine/synctrigger/synctrigger.go now takes an exclusive filelock on path.lock only when the log is full, and checks the size again under the lock. This closes the check-then-rename race that the earlier review flagged as a WARNING.",
              "Failure handling stays best effort. If the lock cannot be acquired within filelock's bound, rotateLog returns and the log keeps growing until the next open. The caller never fails, so the always-exit-0 hook contract is kept. I found no concrete failure mode that this change introduces.",
              "The lock is held only for the removes and renames, and a lock held by a process that dies is released by the OS. The added latency is therefore bounded and applies only to triggers that find a full log.",
              "The new test TestRunChild_ConcurrentTriggersRotateAFullLogOnce in engine/synctrigger/hardening_test.go covers the concurrent rotation case. The review receipt and the task note are documentation only and have no runtime impact."
            ]
          }
        }
