            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "rotateLog now checks full(path) without the lock, takes an exclusive filelock on path.lock, then checks full(path) again before renaming. A trigger that waited on the lock sees the fresh, small log after the first rotation and returns without rotating, so the fresh log is not rotated a second time and no older file is displaced. This addresses the earlier unlocked check-then-rename WARNING.",
              "If the lock cannot be acquired, rotateLog returns without rotating, so the log grows until the next opening. Acquire is called with Perm 0o600. Failure never blocks the sync or loses a line, which fits the always-exit-0, best-effort contract.",
              "The window between the rename and the next open is safe. A concurrent full(path) sees a missing file, stat fails, and it reports not full, so it skips the lock.",
              "TestRunChild_ConcurrentTriggersRotateAFullLogOnce (engine/synctrigger/hardening_test.go:47-80) observes behavior from outside: .1 holds the full log, .2 and .3 hold the older files, and the log has exactly 16 outcome lines. It runs 16 goroutines for 20 rounds, which exercises the race in the way the fix targets, and the task note records RED before and GREEN with -race after.",
              "The lock file is created only when the log is full, so a log under its limit gets none and the goldens are unchanged. The lock is never removed, as the filelock contract requires. The only reliability cost is one leftover 0600 file in the logs directory.",
              "The receipt JSON and the task markdown are documentation and recorded state with no runtime behavior to check."
            ]
          }
        }
